Real hero images (free-stock manual uploads and OpenAI-generated ones —
apps/web/src/app/api/admin/articles/[id]/upload-image/route.ts and
apps/worker/src/generate-image.ts) land here at runtime, served by
apps/web/src/app/uploads/[filename]/route.ts.

Deliberately NOT inside public/ — real gap found and fixed live
2026-09-08: Next.js's `next start` only serves files that existed in
public/ when the server booted; a file written there while the server is
already running 404s until the next restart (confirmed live: the exact
same file served 200 immediately after a plain `docker compose restart
web`, nothing else changed). A real dynamic Route Handler reads the file
from disk on every request instead, so a newly-generated image is
servable immediately with no restart needed. This directory is a
placeholder for local git/dev — infrastructure/docker/docker-compose.yml
mounts a real named volume (uploads_data) over it in production, shared
with apps/worker (which writes here from its own /repo/uploads mount
point on the same volume).
